00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:45,000
constrained by what comes before and after. The cognitive prerequisites for language, hierarchical planning,

126
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:55,000
symbolic thinking, working memory for sequences seem to have been assembling over a long period before anything we'd call language appeared.

127
00:16:55,000 --> 00:17:02,000
By the time you get to Homo sapiens, roughly 300,000 years ago, you have a brain that's been shaped by millions of

128
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:11,000
years of social complexity, gestural communication, vocal communication, and increasingly sophisticated tool making.

129
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:19,000
The neurological infrastructure for language was likely already largely in place before language as we know it existed, which raises a fascinating

